### Test Suite Discrepancy Note (§2c)

- **Scenario A & Scenario B** ([`Tank.test.js:285`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Tank.test.js#L285), [`Tank.test.js:467`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Tank.test.js#L467)): `assert.strictEqual(tank.ns, 1)` (actual `0`, expected `1`):
  - **Reason**: In [`Tank.java`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/decompilation/java-src/Tank.java), the constructor sets `this.ns = 0`. `preform()` never modifies `ns` (only `dosmokes()` increments `ns`), and `reset()` does not touch `ns`. In [`TankProbe.java`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/tools/TankProbe.java), a single `tank` instance was driven sequentially across all test sections. Section 5 tested `dosmokes()`, which incremented `ns` to `1`. When Section 6 ran `reset(40, 1)`, `tank.ns` remained `1` in the Java probe. [`Tank.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Tank.test.js) instantiated a fresh `new Tank(m)` for each scenario without running `dosmokes()`, yet asserted the probe's leftover state `tank.ns = 1`.
  - Per TRANSPILE_SPEC §2c, [`Tank.test.js`](file:///home/evan/resources/ra1/port/Tank.test.js) was left untouched.

